      "section": "Copy number",
      "order": 3,
      "alignment": "left",
      "vertical_alignment": "top",
      "body": "Each point is a 20 kb bin, plotted at its log2 ratio against a diploid baseline, and the thick strokes are the segments a caller made over them: red where the segment reads as a gain, blue as a loss, grey where it is neutral. Read the two together. The gain on chr1 and the loss on chr2 are visible in the log2 track alone, but the chr3 event is not: its total copy number never moves, and only the B-allele frequency underneath shows it, splitting away from 0.5 because the region lost one parental haplotype. Sample, chromosome zoom, axis limit and marker size live in the Settings gear popover.\n",
      "wf_tag": "python/advanced_viz_demo"
    },
